.TH JUDY 3 "2026-08-27" "libexpanse" "Judy Compatibility Manual"
.SH NAME
Judy \- C library for high-performance dynamic arrays (libexpanse compat)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <Judy.h>
.PP
Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBJudy.h\fR provides a 100% source- and binary-compatible drop-in C ABI
replacement for the classic \fBlibjudy\fR library, implemented clean-room
by \fBlibexpanse\fR.
Existing C/C++ applications can swap in \fBlibexpanse\fR with zero source
modifications.
.SH ARRAY TYPES
.TP
.BR Judy1 " (see " Judy1 (3))
Dynamic bit array of machine words (\fBWord_t\fR).
.TP
.BR JudyL " (see " JudyL (3))
Dynamic map from word key (\fBWord_t\fR) to word value (\fBWord_t\fR).
.TP
.BR JudySL " (see " JudySL (3))
Dynamic map from null-terminated string (\fBconst unsigned char *\fR)
to word value.
.TP
.BR JudyHS " (see " JudyHS (3))
Dynamic map from arbitrary byte array (\fBvoid *\fR, \fBWord_t\fR length)
to word value.
.SH DATA TYPES
.TP
.B Word_t, *PWord_t
Unsigned machine word, pointer-sized (64-bit on 64-bit platforms, 32-bit on
32-bit platforms).
.TP
.B Pvoid_t
Opaque pointer representing a Judy array root (initialized to NULL).
.TP
.B PPvoid_t
Pointer to a \fBPvoid_t\fR array pointer (\fBvoid **\fR).
.TP
.B JError_t, *PJError_t
Error diagnostic struct containing \fIje_Errno\fR and \fIje_ErrID\fR.
Pass \fBPJE0\fR (\fBNULL\fR) if error inspection is not required.
.SH ERROR CODES
.nf
.ta 26n 34n
\fBConstant\fR	\fBValue\fR	\fBDescription\fR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
JU_ERRNO_NONE	0	No error
JU_ERRNO_NOMEM	2	Out of memory
JU_ERRNO_NULLPPARRAY	3	Null pointer to array pointer passed
JU_ERRNO_NONNULLPARRAY	4	Array pointer is non-null when expected null
JU_ERRNO_NULLPINDEX	5	Null pointer to index passed
JU_ERRNO_NULLPVALUE	6	Null pointer to value passed
JU_ERRNO_NOTJUDY1	7	Array is not a Judy1 array
JU_ERRNO_NOTJUDYL	8	Array is not a JudyL array
JU_ERRNO_NOTJUDYSL	9	Array is not a JudySL array
JU_ERRNO_UNSORTED	12	Index is unsorted
JU_ERRNO_OVERRUN	13	Index exceeds bounds
JU_ERRNO_CORRUPT	14	Array corruption detected
.fi
.SH MACRO USAGE CONVENTION
Judy provides both raw C functions (\fBJudyLIns\fR, etc.) and shorthand
convenience macros (\fBJLI\fR, \fBJLG\fR, etc.).
The convenience macros automatically pass \fBPJE0\fR as the error parameter.
.PP
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <Judy.h>

int main(void) {
    Pvoid_t PJArray = (Pvoid_t) NULL; /* Root must start as NULL */
    PWord_t PValue;
    Word_t Index;

    /* Insert key 1234 using macro */
    JLI(PValue, PJArray, 1234);
    if (PValue == PJERR) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Out of memory\\n");
        return 1;
    }
    *PValue = 5678; /* Store value */

    /* Retrieve key 1234 */
    JLG(PValue, PJArray, 1234);
    if (PValue) {
        printf("Index 1234 has value %lu\\n", *PValue);
    }

    /* Iterate */
    Index = 0;
    JLF(PValue, PJArray, Index);
    while (PValue != NULL) {
        printf("Index %lu -> %lu\\n", Index, *PValue);
        JLN(PValue, PJArray, Index);
    }

    Word_t BytesFreed;
    JLFA(BytesFreed, PJArray);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH BEHAVIORAL DIFFERENCES FROM ORIGINAL LIBJUDY
.TP
.B Memory Accounting
\fBJudy1MemUsed\fR and \fBJudyLMemUsed\fR report heap consumption. Because
Expanse uses modern cache-aligned 64-byte node structures and custom slab
allocators, exact byte numbers will differ from HP Judy, though asymptotic
scaling remains monotonic and identical.
.TP
.B Out of Memory Handling
\fBAllocation failure aborts the process\fR, following the Rust global-allocator
convention. Functions do \fInot\fR return \fBJERR\fR/\fBPJERR\fR with
\fBJU_ERRNO_NOMEM\fR on exhaustion, so an OOM-recovery branch written against
HP Judy will never be reached here. This is a recorded, deliberate deviation
(doc-gap D3 in the project's compatibility record); \fBJU_ERRNO_NOMEM\fR is
retained in the error enumeration for source compatibility only.
.SH SEE ALSO
